# Ignore file for Dockerfile.admin ONLY. BuildKit reads <Dockerfile name>.dockerignore
# before .dockerignore, and a ROOT .dockerignore also applies to the API and
# maintenance builds, which need db/ (pre-deploy migrations) and widgets/ at runtime:
# the first dev deploy after the panel merge failed its migration for exactly
# that reason. Keep this file named after the Dockerfile.
# Nothing below is needed to compile the admin service, and .env files must
# never reach an image layer.
.git
node_modules
dist
coverage
tests
docs
widgets
snapshots
scripts
db
.github
*.html
*.html.backup
*.md
.env
.env.*
